e Scuola San Marco and an equestrian statue of the mercenary captain Bartolomeo Colleoni (see below)."],["Santa Maria della Pietà","sight",45.4341,12.34493,"Castello","","","","","r","A church that used to house an orphanage and hospital in the 18th century, it is known among classical music enthusiasts as the church where the Catholic priest and composer Antonio Vivaldi worked for most of his career."],["S. Francesco della Vigna","sight",45.4381,12.3486,"Campo San Francesco della Vigna, Castello","08:00-12:00, 16:30-18:00","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["S. Giovanni in Bragora","sight",45.4344,12.347,"Campo Bandiera e Moro, Castello","06:00-11:00, 17:00-19:00","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["S. Maria Formosa","sight",45.4369,12.3411,"Campo Santa Maria Formosa","08:30-12:30, 17:00-19:00","","","","r","The first church dedicated to \"Mary of the Forms\" was built on this spot in the VII century, when the Virgin ordered bishop Magnus to erect one, appearing to him as an exceedingly shapely woman. The current building, planned by Codussi,…"],["S. Zaccaria","sight",45.43472,12.34333,"Campo San Zaccaria","Daily 10:00-12:00, 16:00-18:00","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Byzantine Pictures Museum (Greek Institute)","sight",45.4357,12.34447,"Ponte dei Greci, Castello 3412","09:00-16:30","","","","r","Collection of Greek, Cretan and Venetian icons of the 14th to 18th century."],["Palazzo Grimani","sight",45.43705,12.34241,"Ramo Grimani, Castello 4858","0, Tue-Sun 10:00-19:00, closed Dec 25, Jan 1, May 1","","","","r","A jewel of Renaissance architecture that was opened as a Venetia civic museum in 2008, collections of paintings, archaeological collection of Greek and Roman artefacts, temporary exhibitions."],["Scuola Dalmatina di San Giorgio e Trifone","sight",45.43622,12.34595,"Calle dei Furlani, Castello 3259/A","Tue-Sat 10:00-12:30 and 15:00-18:00, Sun 10:00-12:30, closed Mon","","","","r","Famous painting cycle by Vittore Carpaccio depicting the lives of St.George, Tryphon and Jerome."],["ASAC Library","sight",45.4302,12.3589,"Padiglione centrale, Castello","Tue-Fri 10:00-17:00","","","","r","An annex at the Biennale gardens where the Biennale keeps records related to the Biennale exhibitions and to 20th century art, from 1895 onwards."],["Monument for Giovanni Caboto","sight",45.4319,12.3511,"Via Garibaldi 1581","","","","","r","Venetian explorer of North America who worked for the British (c. 1450-c. 1500)."],["Arsenale","activity",45.43347,12.35058,"","","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Giardini","activity",45.42885,12.35797,"","","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Chiesa della Pietà","activity",45.4341,12.345,"Riva degli Schiavoni","Mon-Sat 19:00","","","","r","Between 1703 and 1740, Antonio Vivaldi taught the orchestra of the girls in the orphanage here, writing unparalleled music for them. Frequent concerts of his Four Seasons by a Baroque ensemble."],["Salvmeria","restaurant",45.43225,12.35251,"Via Giuseppe Garibaldi, 1769","","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Basegó","restaurant",45.43221,12.35233,"Via Giuseppe Garibaldi, 1762","","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Al Giardinetto","restaurant",45.43609,12.34272,"Castello 4928","","","","","r","Just behind the Piazza San Marco, this restaurant has a large private courtyard welcoming guests during good season. Seafood courses and Venetian specialities are served by Severino family."]]}